Severity: ERROR
Category: tigris
Check: config
Fix: Give -l a directory; ship the report another way (tigercron mails it, or copy the file).
References: tigris(8)

The -l option was given @host, which once meant sending the report to
a "logger" on that host over telnet. That feature is gone: it sent the
report, which names the machine's weaknesses, in clear across the
network, and its own test was inverted, so it had never worked. -l
takes a directory the report is written to.
